"""
Keyword rules that decide the ITEM NAME for a product.

How scoring works
-----------------
Each item has a list of (regex, weight) pairs. The regexes run against the
NORMALISED text of  title + category breadcrumb  (lower-case, punctuation turned
into spaces, "&" turned into " and ", apostrophes removed, "-" turned into a space).
The item with the highest score wins.  Specific phrases get higher weights
("liquid lipstick" 9) than generic words ("lipstick" 7, "lip" 2).
A NEGATIVE weight lowers an item's score.

To teach the program something new, just add or edit a line here - no other
file needs to change.
"""

